WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.370
We've been wondering whether Barack Obama
will endorse one of the Democratic primary

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:12.120
candidates for 2020, uh, maybe his former
vice president Biden before the primary is

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.120
over.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.930
And it's not clear that Barack Obama is going
to get involved in this primary, but we now

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.279
have heard from Trump's former advisor, Valerie
Jarrett, who says that number one, Barack

00:00:21.279 --> 00:00:26.759
Obama, his quote, very concerned about what
is going on in the United States, read Trump,

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:32.940
uh, and that he will be getting involved in
the 2020 campaign in some form with the goal

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.660
of ultimately defeating the president, Donald
Trump.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.649
Um, the, let's assume she's right.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:38.649
Okay.

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:41.740
So we're saying this is what Valerie Jarrett
has said.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.530
President Obama thinks, and we'll do, and
I can't imagine she would speak without knowing

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.530
that for a fact.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.510
So let's imagine that it's true for the purposes
of our discussion today.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:56.340
Um, it appears as though Barack Obama does
not plan on getting involved in the primary.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.800
And my thought is that this is the right decision.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.829
And I'm going to tell you why.

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:02.149
I'm guessing Barack Obama understands.

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:08.750
And everybody around Barack Obama understands,
realizes that there's very little upside longterm

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.100
for Democrats of Barack Obama getting involved
in the primary.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:17.160
Now this is not, why didn't Elizabeth Warren
endorsed Bernie during the primary?

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:23.930
If she liked him so much, Obama's relationship
to the presidency and candidates is very different

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.360
than that of Elizabeth Warren's number one.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.649
Uh, Barack Obama was president of the United
States.

00:01:29.649 --> 00:01:34.759
Number two, one of the current Democratic
primary candidates is Barack Obama's former

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:35.759
vice president.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:39.509
So I see this as a no win for Barack Obama
to get involved in the primary.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:45.740
If Obama comes out and endorses Joe Biden,
it furthers the DNC establishment narrative.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.539
It opens up the door to more claims of an
unbalanced primary in which the DNC or quote

00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:53.079
establishment Democrats are meddling.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:58.020
And whether it's true or not, a former president
saying that he wants his former VP to be the

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:04.409
nominee, the election right after the DNC
screwed Bernie in favor of Hillary.

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:05.530
It doesn't look good.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:10.800
So whatever gain might be calculated for Barack
Obama to come out now and endorse Joe Biden,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.220
I think has far more negatives outweighing
it.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:19.990
If Obama not, uh, endorses Biden during the
primary and Biden does not get the nomination,

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:25.050
then there's the question of whether Barack
Obama has weakened the power of his endorsement

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.510
by initially endorsing somebody who doesn't
win.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.130
And then having to go out and campaign for
somebody that he didn't endorse during the

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.250
primary.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.300
If instead of Joe Biden, uh, Barack Obama
prefers somebody else, imagine that Barack

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:42.030
Obama Prefers Bernie Sanders or Elizabeth
Warren or whoever and he endorses them during

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.840
the primary and Biden ends up winning.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.040
Who is of course leading in the polls right
now it's the same problem in reverse.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.490
How strong is Obama Supportive Biden as the
nominee?

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:59.170
If Obama supported Sanders during the primary,
and I understand that many politicians endorse

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.560
one person during the primary, that person
loses, then they support somebody else.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:09.010
It is different when you are a former president
and it is different when one of the candidates

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.760
is your former vice president.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.860
So to me this is fine.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:18.250
Okay, support who you like in the primary
and then you vote to defeat Trump no matter

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:21.430
who the nominee is from the people that are
running.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.920
But the perception of it not going right for
Barack Obama wouldn't be good.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.280
President Obama, imagine that he has built
up a sort of specific amount of political

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.280
capital.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.280
It's a lot.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.280
Okay.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:37.800
The former president who is seen very favorably
by Americans, has a lot of political capital,

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.570
but it's not unlimited political capital.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:44.450
And I don't believe that there is a long term
gain for Barack Obama to get involved in the

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:49.260
primary, in the context of working to defeat
Donald Trump, which is the goal, what Obama

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.870
should do during the primary.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:51.870
It's two things.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.660
Number one, demand and lobby for an open,
transparent primary to the extent that he's

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.840
willing to do that.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.090
And it may not be a significant extent and
I understand that.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.570
And number two, Barack Obama during the primary
should be working to push back against all

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:12.220
of the voter suppression efforts from Republicans
to ensure that when the time comes to vote

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.260
in November of 2020, every vote is counted.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.280
Everyone who wants to vote gets to vote and
have their votes counted, which will help

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.219
the eventual democratic nominee.

00:04:22.219 --> 00:04:27.990
When the time comes for the DNC to formally
nominate the winner of the primary at the

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:33.699
convention, Barack Obama should be there introducing
them and speaking at the DNC and rallying

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:34.699
the troops.

00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:39.139
Uh, but there is not an advantage to him getting
involved at this point in the primary endorsing

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:40.139
somebody.

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:44.710
Now there are some really low energy Beta
comments from Republicans saying that it's

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:49.289
unbecoming of a president, a former president,
to get involved at all in the presidential

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.330
race and that it looks bad.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.330
Gimme a break.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.330
Okay, you're pathetic.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.330
It's unbecoming.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:59.210
To have a president like Trump, embarrassing
the country day in and day out on the national

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.210
stage.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:04.949
Barack Obama is concerned about the future
of this country and he wants to work to change

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:06.139
that trajectory.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:10.689
Or at least according to Valerie Jarrett,
he's planning on working to change that and

00:05:10.689 --> 00:05:12.560
he should be applauded for it.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:20.120
But I completely understand why Barack Obama
is not likely to get involved in this primary.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.439
And I actually agree with that decision for
the strategic reasons that I've outlined.

00:05:24.439 --> 00:05:28.939
If you disagree with my conclusion or if you
simply disagree

00:05:28.939 --> 00:05:31.180
with how I built up that conclusion.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:06:09.960
I want to hear from, I'm on Twitter at the
pacman and the show is on Twitter

